WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.244
An AI assistant can work alongside you on an Orchard Core site.

00:00:05.244 --> 00:00:09.796
In this video, we'll connect one to the Orchard Core MCP server, add

00:00:09.796 --> 00:00:12.810
AI Skills, and see what to ask it to build.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.463
Orchard Core is a large, modular framework.

00:00:20.463 --> 00:00:25.510
Instead of searching the documentation by hand, you can ask an AI assistant

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:32.240
to scaffold modules, write recipes, generate content type migrations, and explain how a feature works.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:37.446
The key to accurate answers is the official Orchard Core MCP server.

00:00:37.446 --> 00:00:43.106
It gives the assistant tool-based access to the Orchard Core documentation, so responses

00:00:43.106 --> 00:00:47.080
reflect how Orchard Core actually works rather than guesses.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.945
AI Skills add a second layer:

00:00:49.945 --> 00:00:55.745
repeatable, Orchard Core specific workflows that guide the assistant through common tasks.

00:00:55.745 --> 00:00:59.250
We'll connect the server first, then add the skills.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:08.829
Model Context Protocol, or MCP, is an open standard that lets AI assistants

00:01:08.829 --> 00:01:11.685
call external tools and data sources.

00:01:11.685 --> 00:01:17.662
The Orchard Core MCP server offers tools that search the Orchard Core documentation,

00:01:17.662 --> 00:01:22.510
so its answers use the correct APIs, module names, and conventions.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:31.271
The server is hosted at ai.orchardcore.net/mcp, and you point any MCP-capable client at this address.

00:01:31.271 --> 00:01:37.110
The assistant then gains access to the Orchard Core tools automatically.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:46.715
GitHub Copilot CLI brings a Copilot coding agent to your terminal.

00:01:46.715 --> 00:01:53.020
Install it with npm, which requires Node.js, then start it by running copilot.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.154
Inside Copilot, run the /mcp add command.

00:01:57.154 --> 00:02:04.138
When prompted, name the server orchardcore, choose the HTTP server type, and enter its URL.

00:02:04.138 --> 00:02:09.898
Or add the server to the Copilot CLI configuration file, where an asterisk

00:02:09.898 --> 00:02:12.850
in the tools key allows every tool.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:19.702
On github.com, open your repository's Settings, choose Copilot, then MCP servers, and add

00:02:19.702 --> 00:02:22.592
the same entry under MCP configuration.

00:02:22.592 --> 00:02:25.289
GitHub requires the tools key there.

00:02:25.289 --> 00:02:30.620
The Copilot cloud agent and code review can then call the Orchard Core tools.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:36.862
In Visual Studio Code, create a .mcp.json file at the root of your

00:02:36.862 --> 00:02:39.837
workspace and add the same entry.

00:02:39.837 --> 00:02:45.940
Its top-level key is mcpServers, as in the Copilot CLI configuration file.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:50.828
Then open the Chat view, select Open Customizations in the title bar, and

00:02:50.828 --> 00:02:52.190
check the Tools tab:

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:55.280
the tools of the orchardcore server are listed there.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.057
Claude Code is a terminal-based AI coding assistant.

00:03:03.057 --> 00:03:07.992
If running claude reports that the command is not recognized or not found,

00:03:07.992 --> 00:03:14.530
install it with npm, which requires Node.js, then verify the installation by asking for its version.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.700
One command registers the server:

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:23.843
claude mcp add, with the transport set to HTTP, the name orchardcore, and the server address.

00:03:23.843 --> 00:03:27.132
Start a session and ask Orchard Core questions:

00:03:27.132 --> 00:03:32.220
the assistant calls the server's tools when it needs Orchard Core knowledge.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.007
In Claude Desktop, remote servers are added as connectors.

00:03:37.007 --> 00:03:43.820
Open Settings, choose Connectors, select Add, then Add custom connector, and enter the server address.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:52.811
Cursor reads an MCP configuration file from your project, or a global one

00:03:52.811 --> 00:03:54.692
from your home directory.

00:03:54.692 --> 00:03:58.270
Here, the entry holds only the address of the server.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:03.378
Any client that supports remote HTTP servers can connect.

00:04:03.378 --> 00:04:09.050
Look for an MCP, Model Context Protocol, or Tools or Connectors setting, and

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:13.200
register an HTTP server with the Orchard Core address.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:23.927
Beyond the MCP server, AI Skills teach an assistant repeatable, Orchard Core specific workflows.

00:04:23.927 --> 00:04:29.494
The documentation links a community project that provides a curated set of skills

00:04:29.494 --> 00:04:32.950
and plugins for building Orchard Core solutions.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:38.074
That project is maintained by the community, and it is not an official

00:04:38.074 --> 00:04:39.628
part of Orchard Core.

00:04:39.628 --> 00:04:43.657
You install it as a plugin for Claude Code or the GitHub Copilot

00:04:43.657 --> 00:04:46.880
CLI, following the instructions in its repository.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:48.984
Use both together.

00:04:48.984 --> 00:04:54.232
The MCP server keeps the assistant grounded in accurate documentation, while the skills

00:04:54.232 --> 00:04:57.730
guide it through common Orchard Core tasks step by step.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:04.615
Once connected, ask in natural language.

00:05:04.615 --> 00:05:08.641
Ask for a module with a Product content type and a price field,

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:13.310
or for a recipe that creates a blog content type, a menu, and a home page.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:18.516
For content modeling, ask for a data migration that adds an AutoroutePart and

00:05:18.516 --> 00:05:20.986
a MarkdownBodyPart to your Article type.

00:05:20.986 --> 00:05:26.247
Because the assistant can consult the documentation through the server, its suggestions stay

00:05:26.247 --> 00:05:28.770
aligned with the framework's conventions.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:33.481
Ask it to explain how display drivers and shapes work, and how to

00:05:33.481 --> 00:05:35.713
customize the rendering of a part.

00:05:35.713 --> 00:05:39.674
Or ask how to handle a content event, to send a notification when

00:05:39.674 --> 00:05:41.180
an item is published.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:44.751
Give the assistant context about your project:

00:05:44.751 --> 00:05:50.175
the modules you have enabled, the content types you use, and your target Orchard Core version.

00:05:50.175 --> 00:05:53.430
Its answers and generated code then fit your solution.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:59.702
The MCP server provides the Orchard Core knowledge, but you remain responsible for the result.

00:05:59.702 --> 00:06:04.120
Review generated code and recipes before you run them in your application.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:13.504
To build the application itself, continue with Create a CMS Web application, Recipes

00:06:13.504 --> 00:06:17.940
and Starter Themes, and Code Generation Templates in the documentation.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:24.720
Connect the Orchard Core MCP server, add AI Skills, give the assistant the

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:28.126
context of your project, and review what it writes.

00:06:28.126 --> 00:06:29.680
Thanks for watching.

